From: Tab5 bring-up
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: esp32p4-i2s CPU DAI driver via AHB GDMA

ESP32-P4 has three I2S units at 0x500c6000+0x1000*n but none owns a
DMA engine: sample data moves through the AHB GDMA at 0x50085000, a
linked-list DMA with 3 TX / 3 RX channels bound to peripherals by the
peri_sel register (I2S0 = 3).

This adds a single-file ASoC driver under sound/soc/espressif that
registers the I2S unit as a CPU DAI and drives one AHB channel per
stream (TX out-ch0, RX in-ch1).  The ring is one lldesc per 4092-byte
chunk with eof on the last chunk of each period, giving one interrupt
per period for snd_pcm_period_elapsed.  Philips/I2S mode runs the TDM
engine with 2 slots + msb_shift like esp-idf does.

Clocks are programmed directly in hp_sys_clkrst: apb gate + module
reset, PLL_160M through an integer divider into the TX/RX module
clocks, mst_clk_sel binds MCLK to the TX clock, and lp_clkrst enables
the MCLK pad.  BCK/WS/DOUT/DIN route through the GPIO matrix from the
espressif,*-pin DT properties.

Only staged for ES_BOARD=tab5 builds (linux/build-m1.sh).

--- a/sound/soc/Kconfig
